    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d673">

                <pb facs="0795" n="1629" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1629"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/356</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3422</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 6, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received June 27.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to this Legation’s telegram
                    No. 3505 of May 30, 1918, transmitting Mr. Dresel’s telegram No. 51 for
                    the War Trade Board,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d673-f1"/> I have the honor to enclose
                    herewith copy and translation of the official communication from the
                    representative of the Swiss Department of Public Economy to the effect that no
                    American cotton will be exported from Switzerland in any form to countries at
                    war with the United States during the life of the agreement of December 5,
                    1917.</p>
                <p>A copy of a personal letter from the head of the Section of Textile Industry of
                    the Department of Public Economy, Dr. E. Iklé, is likewise
                    enclosed. In this letter Dr. Iklé makes the request
                    referred to in the above-mentioned telegram in regard to the form of any public
                    announcement in America concerning this undertaking of the Swiss Government.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pleasant A. Stovall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>




                <xi:include href="d673-a1.xml" xpointer="d673-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d673-a2.xml" xpointer="d673-a2"/>
            </div>
